1
00:00:02,750 --> 00:00:04,790
Here's little Ben nodding off.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,840
Aww, look at Aunt Monica's little boy.

3
00:00:08,040 --> 00:00:11,590
- Look, he's got Ross' haircut.     - Oh, let me see.

4
00:00:12,260 --> 00:00:15,220
Oh, God! Is he just the sweetest thing?

5
00:00:15,430 --> 00:00:18,470
You must just want to kiss him all over.

6
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:24,480
That would be nice.

7
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:28,310
- Pfft.     - Pardon?

8
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:31,860
Nothing. Just a little extra air in my mouth. Pfft.

9
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:40,160
Hey, Chan, can you help me out here? I promise I'll pay you back.

10
00:00:40,370 --> 00:00:43,410
Oh, yeah, right. Including the waffles last week...

11
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:45,250
...you now owe me...

12
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:47,620
...17 jillion dollars.

13
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:50,710
I will, really, I'll pay you back this time.

14
00:00:50,920 --> 00:00:52,800
Where's the money coming from?

15
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:56,550
I'm helping out at the NYU Med School with some, uh, research.

16
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,430
What kind of research?

17
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:02,390
Uh, just, you know, science.

18
00:01:03,060 --> 00:01:04,730
Science.

19
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:08,980
Yeah, I think I've heard of that.

20
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:12,780
It's a fertility study.

21
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:15,940
Joey...

22
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:19,280
Please tell me you're only donating your time.

23
00:01:20,910 --> 00:01:23,240
Come on, you guys. It's not that big a deal.

24
00:01:23,450 --> 00:01:26,210
I just go down there every other day...

25
00:01:26,410 --> 00:01:28,900
...and make my contribution to the project.

26
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:32,670
Hey, but at the end of two weeks, I get $700!

27
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:36,230
Wow, you're gonna be making money hand over fist.

28
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:30,230
Okay, we got the coleslaw. We got the buns.

29
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:34,610
We've got the ground-up flesh of formally cute cows and turkeys.

30
00:02:36,440 --> 00:02:38,360
Men are here!

31
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,580
We make fire.

32
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:48,750
Cook meat.

33
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:51,960
Then put out fire by peeing, no get invited back!

34
00:02:52,210 --> 00:02:53,580
Cute, cute.

35
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:56,670
- Oh, Melanie called. She's gonna be late.     - Oh, okay.

36
00:02:56,880 --> 00:02:58,550
So how are things going with you two?

37
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:01,300
Is she becoming your special someone?

38
00:03:03,510 --> 00:03:05,760
I don't know. She's, uh... She's pretty great.

39
00:03:05,970 --> 00:03:09,180
Yeah? What does she think of your little science project?

40
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:14,560
You think I'm gonna tell a girl I like that I'm also seeing a cup?

41
00:03:18,610 --> 00:03:19,990
The man's got a point.

42
00:03:20,200 --> 00:03:23,860
Well, the tough thing is, she really wants to have sex with me.

43
00:03:24,070 --> 00:03:26,280
Crazy bitch.

44
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:34,880
I still got a week left in the program, and according to the rules...

45
00:03:35,080 --> 00:03:39,000
...if I want to get the money, I'm not allowed to conduct any personal experiments...

46
00:03:39,210 --> 00:03:42,840
- ...if you know what I mean.     - Joey, we always know what you mean.

47
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:51,480
- Hey. Hey.

48
00:03:51,680 --> 00:03:55,020
How long did you think this barbecue was gonna last?

49
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:56,610
I'm going to China.

50
00:03:56,810 --> 00:03:59,440
Jeez, you say one thing and, eh...

51
00:04:00,610 --> 00:04:01,820
You're going to China?

52
00:04:02,030 --> 00:04:04,780
It's, uh, for the museum. Someone found a bone.

53
00:04:04,990 --> 00:04:07,120
We want the bone, they don't want us to have it.

54
00:04:07,330 --> 00:04:11,450
So I'm going to try to persuade them... It's a whole big "bone" thing.

55
00:04:12,910 --> 00:04:15,500
Anyway, I'm gonna be gone for, like, a week.

56
00:04:15,710 --> 00:04:19,800
So, uh, if you wanna reach me, you can't. So here's my itinerary.

57
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,710
Um...

58
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:24,630
- Here's a picture of me.     - Oh, let me see.

59
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:29,390
Could you take it to Carol's now and then and show it to Ben so he doesn't forget me?

60
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:31,810
- Yeah.     - Hi, Ben.

61
00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:33,980
I'm your father.

62
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:39,060
I am The Head! Pahh!

63
00:04:43,820 --> 00:04:45,530
This barbecue's gonna be very fun.

64
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:50,580
Is Rachel here? Um, I wanted to wish her a happy birthday before I left.

65
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:54,000
- Oh, no, she's out having drinks with Carl.     - Oh. Heh.

66
00:04:54,210 --> 00:04:55,960
Hey, who's Carl?

67
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:00,790
- The guy she met at the coffeehouse?     - No.

68
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:05,590
- See, there's this guy she met at...     - The coffeehouse? Right.

69
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,930
So you do know who he is. Heh.

70
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:14,100
I'm gonna go say goodbye to the guys.

71
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:17,190
Hey, you know what? Tell them that bone story.

72
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,400
- Hi.     - Hey.

73
00:05:23,610 --> 00:05:24,610
Hey.

74
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:27,450
- I have to go to China.     - The country?

75
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:32,530
No, this big pile of dishes in my Mom's breakfront.

76
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:36,080
Do you guys know who Carl is?

77
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:39,420
Let's see. Alvin, Simon, Theodore...

78
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:40,790
No.

79
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:44,800
- Well, Rachel's having drinks with him.     - Oh, no!

80
00:05:45,010 --> 00:05:47,550
How can she, when she's never shown interest in you?

81
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:50,890
Forget about her.

82
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,150
He's right, man. Please move on.

83
00:05:53,150 --> 00:05:55,140
Go to China. Eat Chinese food.

84
00:05:55,350 --> 00:05:58,190
Of course, there they just call it food.

85
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:02,270
Yeah? I guess. I don't know.

86
00:06:03,110 --> 00:06:06,400
All right, just give her this for me, okay?

87
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:08,450
Listen, we're just looking out for you.

88
00:06:08,650 --> 00:06:10,160
- I know.     - We want you to be happy.

89
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:14,240
And I may only have a couple beers in me, but I love you, man.

90
00:06:16,790 --> 00:06:18,660
I'm still on my first.

91
00:06:21,630 --> 00:06:23,290
I just think you're nice.

92
00:06:30,640 --> 00:06:34,390
Anyway, that's when me and my friends started this fruit-basket business.

93
00:06:34,600 --> 00:06:39,180
We call ourselves "The Three Basketeers." Ha, ha.

94
00:06:39,390 --> 00:06:42,270
Like "The Three Musketeers," only with fruit.

95
00:06:43,770 --> 00:06:44,980
Oh!

96
00:06:46,030 --> 00:06:47,280
Okay.

97
00:06:49,110 --> 00:06:52,860
- How do you like your burgers?     - No. Presents first, food later!

98
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:55,450
Hold on there, tiger.

99
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:57,830
How's it going? How you holding up?

100
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,540
Well, not so good.

101
00:06:59,750 --> 00:07:03,130
She thinks tonight's the night we're gonna complete the transaction...

102
00:07:03,330 --> 00:07:04,710
...if you know what I...

103
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,380
And you do. Heh.

104
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,220
So, uh, have you ever thought about being there for her?

105
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:12,220
What do you mean?

106
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:18,720
You know, just be there for her.

107
00:07:21,390 --> 00:07:22,940
Not following you.

108
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:28,150
Think about it.

109
00:07:32,950 --> 00:07:38,370
Okay, I'm guessing this is from...

110
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:43,170
Well, thank you, Melanie.

111
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:45,960
- Okay, this one right here is from me.     - Okay.

112
00:07:46,170 --> 00:07:47,750
Hmm. Ah, it's light.

113
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:51,300
It rattles. It's...

114
00:07:53,010 --> 00:07:56,600
- ...Travel Scrabble.     - Ha, ha, hey!

115
00:07:57,220 --> 00:08:00,180
Wow. Thank you.

116
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,310
This one's from Joey.

117
00:08:05,520 --> 00:08:10,400
It feels like a book. I think it's a book. Feels like a book. And it's a book!

118
00:08:10,610 --> 00:08:12,400
It's Dr. Seuss!

119
00:08:13,650 --> 00:08:16,320
That book got me through some tough times.

120
00:08:17,780 --> 00:08:20,370
There is a little child inside this man.

121
00:08:20,580 --> 00:08:24,200
The doctors say if they remove it, he'll die.

122
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:28,500
- Who's this from?     - That's, uh, Ross'.

123
00:08:28,710 --> 00:08:29,960
Ah.

124
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:36,550
Oh, my God.

125
00:08:37,600 --> 00:08:38,890
He remembered.

126
00:08:39,100 --> 00:08:40,310
Remembered what?

127
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,220
It was, like, months ago.

128
00:08:42,430 --> 00:08:45,940
We were walking by this antique store, and I saw this pin in the window.

129
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:49,810
I told him it was just like one my grandmother had when I was little.

130
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:53,360
Aw! I can't believe he remembered!

131
00:08:53,570 --> 00:08:57,160
Well, sure, but can you play it on a plane?

132
00:09:01,290 --> 00:09:04,250
Oh, it's so pretty.

133
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:07,420
- This must've cost him a fortune.     - I can't believe he did this.

134
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:09,960
Ross? Remember when he fell in love with Carol...

135
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:13,990
...and bought her that ridiculously expensive crystal duck?

136
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:16,550
What did you just say?

137
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:30,020
Crystal duck.

138
00:09:34,280 --> 00:09:36,530
No, no, no.

139
00:09:36,740 --> 00:09:39,910
The, um... The "love" part?

140
00:09:46,370 --> 00:09:49,370
Oh, my God.

141
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:52,790
Oh, no, no, no, no.

142
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:55,300
That's good. Just keep rubbing your head.

143
00:09:55,510 --> 00:09:57,970
That'll turn back time.

144
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:06,770
This is unbelievable. I mean, this is unbelievable.

145
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:09,640
I know. This is really, really huge.

146
00:10:09,850 --> 00:10:14,320
No, it's not. It's small, it's tiny, it's petite, it's wee.

147
00:10:14,780 --> 00:10:19,530
Uh-uh. I don't think any of our lives will ever be the same ever again.

148
00:10:20,910 --> 00:10:23,490
Is there a mute button on this woman?

149
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:27,120
I think this is so great! I mean, you and Ross!

150
00:10:27,330 --> 00:10:30,580
- Did you have any idea?     - No, none.

151
00:10:30,790 --> 00:10:34,090
My first night in the city, he mentioned asking me out...

152
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,760
...but nothing ever happened, so I just...

153
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:40,130
What else did he say? Does he want to go out with me?

154
00:10:40,340 --> 00:10:42,510
Given that he's desperately in love with you...

155
00:10:42,720 --> 00:10:45,810
...he wouldn't mind getting a cup of coffee or something.

156
00:10:46,560 --> 00:10:47,770
Ross?

157
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:50,100
All this time?

158
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,690
- I've gotta talk to him.     - He's in China!

159
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,020
The country.

160
00:10:55,820 --> 00:10:58,610
Wait, his flight doesn't leave for 45 minutes.

161
00:10:58,820 --> 00:11:01,400
What about the time difference? From here to the airport?

162
00:11:01,610 --> 00:11:02,660
Yes!

163
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:06,530
- You're never gonna make it!     - I've got to try.

164
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:08,660
What are you gonna say to him?

165
00:11:08,870 --> 00:11:10,160
I don't know.

166
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:11,830
Maybe you shouldn't go.

167
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:14,920
Right, because if you're gonna break his heart, that can wait.

168
00:11:15,130 --> 00:11:17,750
Yeah, but if it's good news, tell him now.

169
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,460
Maybe I'll know when I see him.

170
00:11:19,670 --> 00:11:22,180
Here, look. All right, does this help?

171
00:11:28,770 --> 00:11:30,020
No.

172
00:11:30,230 --> 00:11:34,190
All I know is, I cannot wait a week. This is just too big.

173
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,820
I've just got to talk to him. I've got...

174
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:39,400
- I'll see you later.     - Rachel, I love you!

175
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:42,880
Deal with me first!

176
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:55,750
All right.

177
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:01,880
Ross! Ross.

178
00:12:02,090 --> 00:12:03,170
Excuse me, pardon me.

179
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:04,840
- Hi. Your boarding pass?     - Hi.

180
00:12:05,050 --> 00:12:06,890
No, I need to talk to my friend.

181
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:11,060
Sorry, you're not allowed on the jetway unless you have a boarding pass.

182
00:12:11,270 --> 00:12:14,480
He just went on. He's right there, in the blue jacket! Can I just...?

183
00:12:14,690 --> 00:12:16,650
I'm sorry. Federal regulations!

184
00:12:16,860 --> 00:12:20,860
All right, um, then could you please just give him a message for me?

185
00:12:21,070 --> 00:12:22,610
Please? This is very important.

186
00:12:22,820 --> 00:12:25,160
All right. What's the message?

187
00:12:25,490 --> 00:12:27,870
Uh... I don't know.

188
00:12:30,450 --> 00:12:32,790
Excuse me! Sir! Excuse me! Sir?

189
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:34,910
- I have a message for you.     - What?

190
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:39,000
It's from Rachel. She loved the present. She'll see you when you get back.

191
00:12:39,210 --> 00:12:40,920
What?

192
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:45,050
Toby, I don't know what she's talking about.

193
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:46,760
There's no Rachel!

194
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:49,140
Don't give me that deep freeze!

195
00:12:58,520 --> 00:13:02,280
Oh, Joey, Joey, Joey!

196
00:13:03,030 --> 00:13:06,030
I think I blacked out there for a minute.

197
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:09,160
It was nothing.

198
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:13,950
Well, now we gotta find something fun for you!

199
00:13:17,370 --> 00:13:19,670
Ahh, you know what?

200
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:24,590
Forget about me. Let's, uh... Let's give you another turn.

201
00:13:27,010 --> 00:13:28,430
Me, again?

202
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:30,970
Sure. Why not?

203
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:38,980
Boy! Somebody's gonna get a big fruit basket tomorrow!

204
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:48,200
I gotta tell you, you are nothing like I thought you would be.

205
00:13:48,410 --> 00:13:49,740
How do you mean?

206
00:13:49,950 --> 00:13:54,290
I just had you pegged as one of those guys who are always, "Me, me, me!"

207
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,040
- Ha, ha.     - But you...

208
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:58,950
...you're a giver.

209
00:13:59,630 --> 00:14:02,040
You're, like, the most generous man I ever met.

210
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:06,310
I mean, you're practically a woman.

211
00:14:12,100 --> 00:14:14,890
So, uh, Rach, do you want to save this wrapping paper?

212
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:16,390
It's only a little torn.

213
00:14:16,600 --> 00:14:19,940
Are you gonna go for it with Ross, or should I throw it out?

214
00:14:22,770 --> 00:14:26,030
I don't know. I don't know.

215
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:29,200
Thought about it all of the way there...

216
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:32,570
...and I thought about it all the way back and, uh...

217
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,530
You know, it's Ross!

218
00:14:34,740 --> 00:14:37,040
You know what I mean? It's Ross.

219
00:14:37,250 --> 00:14:38,870
- Sure!     - Sure.

220
00:14:39,330 --> 00:14:44,000
I don't know. This is just my initial gut feeling...

221
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,880
...but I'm thinking...

222
00:14:47,880 --> 00:14:49,050
...it'd be really great.

223
00:14:49,260 --> 00:14:52,840
Oh, my God, me too! Oh, we'd be like friends-in-law!

224
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:57,310
The best part is you already know everything about him.

225
00:14:57,520 --> 00:14:59,640
It's like starting on the 15th date.

226
00:14:59,850 --> 00:15:03,310
But it would be like starting on the 15th date.

227
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:06,110
Another good point.

228
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:07,900
No, I mean...

229
00:15:08,110 --> 00:15:12,530
At the 15th date, you're already in a "relationship-y" place.

230
00:15:12,740 --> 00:15:14,450
You're committed.

231
00:15:15,410 --> 00:15:17,040
Huh.

232
00:15:17,490 --> 00:15:19,830
What happens if it doesn't work out?

233
00:15:20,040 --> 00:15:23,040
- Why isn't it working out?     - I don't know, sometimes it doesn't.

234
00:15:23,250 --> 00:15:26,960
Is he not cute enough for you? Does he not make enough money?

235
00:15:27,170 --> 00:15:29,340
- No, I'm just...     - Maybe there's someone else.

236
00:15:29,550 --> 00:15:32,220
Is there? Is there someone else?

237
00:15:32,430 --> 00:15:35,600
- No, there is no one else.     - Then why the hell...

238
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:38,180
- ...are you dumping my brother?     - Wha...?

239
00:15:48,570 --> 00:15:49,980
- Hey, big...     - Shh!

240
00:15:50,190 --> 00:15:51,900
Spender.

241
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,740
She's still asleep.

242
00:15:55,950 --> 00:15:58,450
- So how'd it go?     - It was amazing.

243
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:00,700
You know how you think you're great in bed?

244
00:16:00,910 --> 00:16:04,580
The fact you'd even ask shows how little you know me.

245
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:07,880
Well, it's like, last night I couldn't do the thing...

246
00:16:08,090 --> 00:16:10,000
...that usually makes me great.

247
00:16:10,210 --> 00:16:12,340
So I had to do all this other stuff.

248
00:16:12,550 --> 00:16:15,590
And the response I got! Man, oh, man.

249
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:17,970
It was like a ticker-tape parade!

250
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:23,560
Yes I know. As it happens, my room is very close to the parade route.

251
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:33,030
It was amazing, and not just for her. Uh-uh. For me too.

252
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:36,320
It's like, all of a sudden, I'm blind...

253
00:16:36,530 --> 00:16:38,700
...but all my other senses are heightened.

254
00:16:38,910 --> 00:16:42,540
You know? It's like, I was able to appreciate it...

255
00:16:42,750 --> 00:16:44,790
...on another level.

256
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:49,840
I didn't know you had another level.

257
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,170
I know. Neither did I!

258
00:17:01,680 --> 00:17:03,930
- Hey, great skirts! Birthday present?     - Yeah.

259
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:05,730
- From who?     - From you.

260
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:08,060
I exchanged the blouse you got me.

261
00:17:09,770 --> 00:17:11,360
Well, it's the thought.

262
00:17:12,190 --> 00:17:14,690
Doesn't Ross' flight get in in a couple hours?

263
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:16,740
At gate 27B?

264
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:19,870
Uh, yeah.

265
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:22,540
Monica, you know, I've been thinking about it.

266
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:26,120
I've decided this Ross thing is not a good idea.

267
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:28,170
- Why?     - Because I feel...

268
00:17:28,380 --> 00:17:30,920
...like I wouldn't just be going out with him.

269
00:17:31,130 --> 00:17:33,210
I would be going out with all of you.

270
00:17:33,420 --> 00:17:37,010
- Ugh, there'd be all this pressure and...     - No pressure, no pressure!

271
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:41,800
Nothing has even happened yet and you're already so...

272
00:17:42,010 --> 00:17:43,350
I'm not "so."

273
00:17:43,560 --> 00:17:45,770
I was a teensy bit weird at first...

274
00:17:45,980 --> 00:17:48,850
...but I'll be good. I promise.

275
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:55,150
Who is it?

276
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:56,690
It's me, Carl.

277
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:57,990
Come on up.

278
00:17:58,200 --> 00:17:59,950
Behind my brother's back?

279
00:18:01,530 --> 00:18:05,840
Is the kind of crazy thing you won't be hearing from me.

280
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:22,140
- Seven hundred bucks.     - All right, you did it.

281
00:18:22,350 --> 00:18:23,720
Do we have any fruit?

282
00:18:26,850 --> 00:18:28,810
Man, hell of a two weeks, huh?

283
00:18:29,020 --> 00:18:32,020
You know what, though? I really feel I learned something.

284
00:18:32,230 --> 00:18:34,860
So you'll stick with this "it's all for her" thing?

285
00:18:35,070 --> 00:18:36,860
What, are you crazy?

286
00:18:37,070 --> 00:18:41,450
When a blind man gets his sight back, does he walk around like this?

287
00:18:46,910 --> 00:18:50,290
I'm just saying, if I see one more picture of Ed Begley Jr...

288
00:18:50,500 --> 00:18:52,540
...in that stupid electric car...

289
00:18:52,750 --> 00:18:54,250
...I'm gonna shoot myself!

290
00:18:56,460 --> 00:19:00,220
Don't get me wrong. I'm not against environmental issues, per se...

291
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:02,180
...it's just that guy!

292
00:19:02,390 --> 00:19:06,600
I can't believe you'd rather go out with him than me.

293
00:19:06,810 --> 00:19:10,020
Excuse me, please. I'm trying to have a date here.

294
00:19:10,230 --> 00:19:13,190
Fine, just stop thinking about me.

295
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:18,400
Can't do it, can you?

296
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,530
So I'm thinking about you. So what?

297
00:19:21,820 --> 00:19:24,950
I don't get it. What do you see in this guy anyway?

298
00:19:25,160 --> 00:19:28,540
Well, he seems to be a very nice guy.

299
00:19:28,750 --> 00:19:32,470
I mean, come on, buddy! Get a real car!

300
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:38,590
Rachel, come on. Give us a chance.

301
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:41,220
- Ross, it's too hard.     - No, no.

302
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,340
Because it'll get weird for everyone else?

303
00:19:43,550 --> 00:19:45,720
Who cares about them? This is about us.

304
00:19:45,930 --> 00:19:49,430
I've been in love with you since the ninth grade.

305
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:52,190
- You're, like, my best friend.     - I know.

306
00:19:52,390 --> 00:19:54,350
- If we broke up, and I lost you...     - Whoa.

307
00:19:54,560 --> 00:19:56,400
Why do you think we'll break up?

308
00:19:56,610 --> 00:20:00,480
Have you been involved with someone where you haven't broken up?

309
00:20:03,030 --> 00:20:04,700
No.

310
00:20:04,910 --> 00:20:08,620
But it only has to happen once.

311
00:20:08,950 --> 00:20:12,000
You and I know we are perfect for each other.

312
00:20:12,290 --> 00:20:13,410
Right?

313
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:17,290
So the only question is: Are you attracted to me?

314
00:20:19,380 --> 00:20:21,210
I don't know.

315
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:25,760
I mean, I've never looked at you that way before.

316
00:20:26,680 --> 00:20:28,140
Well start looking.

317
00:20:38,610 --> 00:20:39,650
Wow.

318
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:41,070
Exactly!

319
00:20:41,280 --> 00:20:43,190
And you just know I'm gonna be the guy...

320
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:46,360
...caught behind this hammerhead in traffic!

321
00:20:48,990 --> 00:20:50,200
- Right.     - Heh.

322
00:20:50,410 --> 00:20:52,080
You're right.

323
00:20:52,450 --> 00:20:53,540
- You know what?     - What?

324
00:20:53,910 --> 00:20:57,040
I forgot, I'm supposed to pick up a friend at the airport.

325
00:20:57,250 --> 00:20:59,380
I am so sorry. I'm so...

326
00:20:59,590 --> 00:21:02,960
If you want to stay and finish your drinks, please do.

327
00:21:03,170 --> 00:21:05,590
I'm sorry, I gotta go. I'm sorry.

328
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,510
But...

329
00:21:16,980 --> 00:21:18,940
Excuse me! Pardon me! Excuse me.

330
00:21:19,150 --> 00:21:20,770
I'm sorry. Ha, ha.

331
00:21:20,980 --> 00:21:23,820
Toby, for God's sake, will you let it go?

332
00:21:24,030 --> 00:21:25,780
There's no Rachel!

333
00:21:30,620 --> 00:21:33,790
- Oh, hey. I got that.     - Oh.

334
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:36,500
- Thanks, sweetie.     - No problem.

335
00:21:42,340 --> 00:21:44,760
I cannot wait for you to meet my friends.

336
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:47,510
Really? You don't think they'll judge and ridicule me?

337
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:49,510
No, they will. I just, uh...

338
00:21:49,720 --> 00:21:51,010
- Can't wait. Heh.     - Can't wait.

339
00:21:51,220 --> 00:21:52,760
Come on, they're gonna love you.

